# Highly Available 3-Tier Web Application with Amazon RDS, ALB & Auto Scaling on AWS

A production-style, fault-tolerant 3-tier web application deployed on **AWS (`us-east-1`)** integrating **Amazon EC2 (Ubuntu + Apache2/PHP)**, a private **Amazon RDS (MySQL)** database tier, an **Application Load Balancer (ALB)**, and an **EC2 Auto Scaling Group (ASG)** inside a custom VPC.

## Cloud Architecture Diagram

```text
                        [ Internet Users ]
                                │
                                ▼
             [ Internet-Facing Application Load Balancer ]
                        (project-LB | HTTP:80)
                                │
                                ▼
                    [ Target Group: target ]
                                │
        ┌───────────────────────┴───────────────────────┐
        ▼                                               ▼
[ EC2 Web/App Instance 1 ]                     [ EC2 Web/App Instance 2 ]
 (Ubuntu | Apache2 + PHP)                       (Ubuntu | Apache2 + PHP)
        └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                ▲               │ (TCP Port 3306)
                │               ▼
[ EC2 Auto Scaling Group ]   [ Amazon RDS: MySQL 5.7 ]
 (Min: 1 | Des: 2 | Max: 3)   (Private Subnet | Public Access: No)
```

## Implementation Highlights
- **Web & Application Tier (EC2 + Apache2/PHP):** Provisioned an Ubuntu `c5a.large` instance (`project1`), configured Apache2 web services under `/var/www/html`, and deployed a PHP web form connected to the backend database[cite: 15, 17, 18, 22, 23].
- **Private Managed Database Tier (Amazon RDS):** Deployed a MySQL `5.7.44` RDS instance (`intel`) with public access disabled (`Publicly accessible: No`), restricting ingress on port `3306` exclusively to the VPC security group (`sg-050eb5817ad82876f`)[cite: 20, 21].
- **Load Balancing & Auto Scaling:** Created an HTTP Target Group (`target`)[cite: 27], an Internet-facing Application Load Balancer (`project-LB`), and a reusable Launch Template (`mytemplate`)[cite: 30, 31] powering an Auto Scaling Group (`auto-scale`, capacity `1–3`) verified at `2/2 Healthy` instances.

